From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:52:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: arm: google: Document the soc_id property

The bootloaders of the gs101 and gs201 Pixels pick the base DTB by a
root soc_id property: they combine the SoC's product id register with
its major revision register and compare the result with the property's
first cell. Google's base device trees carry it as two cells, the
second zero, and so do the gs101 and gs201 boards here (oriole, raven,
cheetah, felix, panther); without it ABL rejects the DTB.

The schema didn't describe it, so dtbs_check couldn't decode it and
reported it on every one of those boards:

  gs201-felix.dtb: / (google,gs201-felix): soc_id:
    b'\t\x85P\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00' is not of type 'object', 'integer',
    'array', 'boolean', 'null'

Describe it next to soc_compatible, which the zuma boards and the
Pixel 7a use instead.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/gs201/+/606d4345bc0dc66e3bc0a8deaa97cc288bbf53d1/dts/gs201-b0.dts
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/gs101/+/51aa290c65e62f169eff2d12ebdd355354d7d966/dts/gs101-b0.dts
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/google.yaml | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/google.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/google.yaml
index a05273275..988cf3de0 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/google.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/google.yaml
@@ -74,6 +74,18 @@ properties:
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
         description: Size of the ECT in bytes.
 
+  soc_id:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description:
+      Bootloaders that match on this property rather than /soc_compatible
+      (gs101's and gs201's) pick the base DTB whose first cell equals the
+      SoC's product id combined with its major revision.
+    items:
+      - description:
+          The SoC's product id ORed with its major revision, for example
+          0x09855001 for gs201 B0.
+      - description: Reserved, zero in the vendor's device trees.
+
   soc_compatible:
     type: object
     description:
